{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends","id":425677,"title":"Who's getting psyched for Sothis Ascends?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-02T14:33:59-08:00","id":425677,"title":"Who's getting psyched for Sothis Ascends?","content":"And what are you hoping is contained within it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T14:43:42-08:00","id":425698,"title":"","content":"My Mummy group is quite looking forward to the first bit of content for them since Guildhalls of the Deathless. They're mostly just hoping for new Affinities/Utterances to pore over. As their GM, I would quite like expansion on certain antagonist elements. Overall, I think my personal big three wishes are:<br /> <br /> 1. Relic Architecture. I think DC promised to explore this in a future supplement, and my Tef-Aabhi player would kill for it.<br /> 2. More Bane stuff. Bane Relics in particular. I have one written up as the crux of a central plot point in my current game, but more exploration of this idea would be great.<br /> 3. Rules for mortal sorcerers. This is in last place for me, because worst-case scenario I can use Seba to approximate that effect. But given how many hints the game line has regarding these sorcerers, an expansion on who they are and where they stand in Mummy cosmology would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T15:07:47-08:00","id":425715,"title":"","content":"NON-IREMITE MUMMIES!<br /> <br /> 90% of my hope for the book right there. That, along with moral sorcerers and the Roman \u00c6gyptus setting will sell me on this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T15:19:39-08:00","id":425718,"title":"","content":"Eh... I'll actually be a little disappointed if they waste word count on non-Iremite Mummies. We already have plenty of options in that department (Twice-Arisen, Shuankhsen/Deceived, anything spawned by a Blasphemous Depiction-esque relic). I'm not really hankering for mechanics in that department.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:26:45-08:00","id":425759,"title":"","content":"Where were mortal sorcerers mentioned? I think I missed something on my reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:48:10-08:00","id":425768,"title":"","content":"There are references to Sekhem-wielding sorcerers scattered throughout a lot of Mummy books, usually as throwaway lines. The one that most immediately leaps to mind is in Guildhalls of the Deathless in the table where it lists what Talisman powers can be accessed by beings other than the Talisman's creator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:24:14-08:00","id":425821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=425715#post425715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NON-IREMITE MUMMIES!<br /> <br /> 90% of my hope for the book right there. That, along with moral sorcerers and the Roman \u00c6gyptus setting will sell me on this book.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do you mean you want Mummies that have adapted strongly to other cultures or you want non Irem Rite of Return Deathless because if the later don't get your hopes up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:01:24-08:00","id":426026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=425821#post425821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do you mean you want Mummies that have adapted strongly to other cultures or you want non Irem Rite of Return Deathless because if the later don't get your hopes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's been pretty explicit mention of later attempts at the Rite failing or creating Lifeless. I'd love to see some of those Lifeless, especially with less emphasis on Iremite/Egyptian trappings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:07:07-08:00","id":426042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426026#post426026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's been pretty explicit mention of later attempts at the Rite failing or creating Lifeless. I'd love to see some of those Lifeless, especially with less emphasis on Iremite/Egyptian trappings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the desire for more antagonists and the like, but the wish for things with fewer Iremite trappings just feels bizarre. A big part of Mummy is about legacy, both the legacy of your own actions and the legacy of Irem in general. Wishing for Mummy to include things without a connection to Irem feels like wishing for Vampire expansions that don't have anything to do with blood. If new kinds of Lifeless do get written up, I actually hope they are mainly products of later Egyptian sorcerers with a direct connection to Irem.<br /> <br /> If you want Mummies without Irem, that's what the Blue Books (specifically, Immortals) are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:12:36-08:00","id":426044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426042#post426042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the desire for more antagonists and the like, but the wish for things with fewer Iremite trappings just feels bizarre. A big part of Mummy is about legacy, both the legacy of your own actions and the legacy of Irem in general. Wishing for Mummy to include things without a connection to Irem feels like wishing for Vampire expansions that don't have anything to do with blood. If new kinds of Lifeless do get written up, I actually hope they are mainly products of later Egyptian sorcerers with a direct connection to Irem.<br /> <br /> If you want Mummies without Irem, that's what the Blue Books (specifically, Immortals) are for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like challenging the Arisen's inherent sense of cultural exceptionalism is a theme worth exploring. Yes, Irem did incredible things, things that haven't been matched since. But showing that other people have gotten close, that others have grasped at the same ideas? That's a paradigm shakeup that could fuel incredible stories. It's not like the idea of bringing the dead back is unique; other cultures could've explored the same idea and failed (or created Lifeless) without directly copying Iremite methods, and that's uncanny enough to be really, really cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:39:17-08:00","id":426060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426044#post426044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like challenging the Arisen's inherent sense of cultural exceptionalism is a theme worth exploring. Yes, Irem did incredible things, things that haven't been matched since. But showing that other people have gotten close, that others have grasped at the same ideas? That's a paradigm shakeup that could fuel incredible stories. It's not like the idea of bringing the dead back is unique; other cultures could've explored the same idea and failed (or created Lifeless) without directly copying Iremite methods, and that's uncanny enough to be really, really cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that, as written, Irem <i>was</i> exceptional. Anyone who ends up creating Lifeless was probably mimicking the Rite of Return using lost lore from Irem passed down and diluted over the centuries. And that's good for Mummy, because that makes everything personal. You, along with every antagonist you encounter, owes something to Ancient Irem.<br /> <br /> This isn't something unusual for a game line, I should add. There is precious little in Werewolf that doesn't relate to Spirits, or Changeling to the Fae, or Geist to the Underworld. The only part where Mummy stands apart to those lines is that it has the singular honour of having a... &quot;source&quot;, for lack of a better word, that comes bundled with a lot of very specific cultural trappings.<br /> <br /> As I said, if you want something spooky to throw at the players that is outside of the norm for their game line, that is what blue book monsters (or other game lines) are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:59:30-08:00","id":426074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426026#post426026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's been pretty explicit mention of later attempts at the Rite failing or creating Lifeless. I'd love to see some of those Lifeless, especially with less emphasis on Iremite/Egyptian trappings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is not the same thing as getting more Mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T20:16:07-08:00","id":426100,"title":"","content":"Lifeless Mummies created by other cultures are still thematically relevant to the game because they make an Arisen ask, &quot;Hey, wait. If they can do it, what makes our Judges so great?&quot; In all honesty, that kind of realization is what made me an atheist so long ago: &quot;If there's all these differing religions and gods out there what makes the one I believe The Only Correct One?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's what another culture's mummies and sorceries would do for the Arisen. Anything that casts doubt on their purpose is good story-telling for corpses whose story is about freedom from the Judges and the lack thereof","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T20:26:25-08:00","id":426110,"title":"","content":"Except we already have that. Most Arisen don't know what the Shuankhsen are, and Ammut ensures that lack of knowledge is perpetuated. One of the theories bandied around by the Arisen is that the Shuankhsen are failed attempts at emulating the Rite of Return by later cultures, and the fact that Shuankhsen appear in whatever corpse is nearby helps add almost a degree of authenticity to that. If you want to run a story about a Mummy having their faith in their Judges shaken by the actions of one of the Lifeless, well, you've already got an antagonist type that would take great joy in doing just that.<br /> <br /> And I don't think making the Arisen query the Judges on the grounds of metaphysical superiority is actually in keeping with the game's themes. Arisen should spurn the Judges because they want self-determination and freedom from what is tantamount to mystical slavery and enforced dementia, not because their gods might not be as powerful as some other gods that also made magic slaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T20:41:18-08:00","id":426121,"title":"","content":"I didn't really mean it like they should question the Judges because they aren't as strong as other gods. Really, you could just twist these Lifeless Mummies into promoting the themes that you said (and that I meant to imply): who are these other Mummies and why do they seem free and unbound from mystical slavery?<br /> <br /> All I'm saying is that the game has a lot of wiggle room and plenty of growing space, and plenty of themes that new, flashy antagonists can ride on.<br /> <br /> At the very least, what is it you feel is missing from the game? You we don't need 'strange Mummies' since we can use <b>Immortals</b>, but you say you want mortal sorcerers; the argument I always hear against that, though, is that we have <b>Second Sight</b>, <b>Mage the Awakening</b>, and <b>Witch-finders</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T20:54:11-08:00","id":426129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426121#post426121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't really mean it like they should question the Judges because they aren't as strong as other gods. Really, you could just twist these Lifeless Mummies into promoting the themes that you said (and that I meant to imply): who are these other Mummies and why do they seem free and unbound from mystical slavery?</div> </div> </div> </div>In which case they're kind of filling the same niche as Mummies who have achieved Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426121#post426121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I'm saying is that the game has a lot of wiggle room and plenty of growing space, and plenty of themes that new, flashy antagonists can ride on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree, but I don't find non-Egyptian Mummies to be particularly good antagonists that play into Mummy's themes. It depends on the execution, of course, but the concept isn't something that appears to work in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426121#post426121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, what is it you feel is missing from the game? You we don't need 'strange Mummies' since we can use <b>Immortals</b>, but you say you want mortal sorcerers; the argument I always hear against that, though, is that we have <b>Second Sight</b>, <b>Mage the Awakening</b>, and <b>Witch-finders</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the difference. Mortal sorcerers, when mentioned in the books, are mentioned as operating using the lost lore of Irem and wielding Sekhem to fuel their power. This explicitly ties them into Irem's legacy and ties them to Mummy's metaphysics. On the flipside, all the requests for other forms of Mummy invariably seem to come bundled with the request that they be non-Iremite and created independently of Irem. That makes them as much a part of the Mummy setting, from the sound of it, as anything published in a blue book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:04:49-08:00","id":426136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426100#post426100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lifeless Mummies created by other cultures are still thematically relevant to the game because they make an Arisen ask, &quot;Hey, wait. If they can do it, what makes our Judges so great?&quot; In all honesty, that kind of realization is what made me an atheist so long ago: &quot;If there's all these differing religions and gods out there what makes the one I believe The Only Correct One?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's what another culture's mummies and sorceries would do for the Arisen. Anything that casts doubt on their purpose is good story-telling for corpses whose story is about freedom from the Judges and the lack thereof</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly fine for someone's tabletop. Doesn't mean it's good for the game. And given what we've seen on Arisen attitudes about Lifeless. I'm much much more inclined to see them think the exact opposite of what you're trying to suggest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:27:42-08:00","id":426147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426136#post426136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's certainly fine for someone's tabletop. Doesn't mean it's good for the game. And given what we've seen on Arisen attitudes about Lifeless. I'm much much more inclined to see them think the exact opposite of what you're trying to suggest.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Everything is either from Irem and awesome or not from Irem and shitty&quot; gets boring, much in the same way that Mage 1e suffered from &quot;everything is Atlantis.&quot; There's more to the world than the Nameless Empire and the 'failures' that have come since, and exploring some of that has a lot of potential. Sekhem is a <i>universal force</i>; Irem shouldn't have a monopoly on it, and certainly shouldn't be the only group of humans (or whatever the Shan'iatu were) to consciously interact with it. Show me what the rest of humankind has done in the ~6000 years we've had since Irem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:40:22-08:00","id":426156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426147#post426147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Everything is either from Irem and awesome or not from Irem and shitty&quot; gets boring</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a value judgement and we're going to have to agree to disagree over it. Every other game line is about creatures that are scattered across the world in roughly even numbers with mysterious origin sources that may be fact or fiction and are, in either case, tied to no real world geography. Mummy is different. Irem is the grandfather of civilisation, the world's only great magical empire, and was ruled by demigods. It was also definitively situated in pre-Dynastic Egypt and steeped in the trappings of Egyptian magic. No other civilisation had the &quot;advantage&quot; of being ruled by beings like the Shan'iatu with a direct line to the very gods themselves, and the fact remains that the Rite of Return (and actions of the Deceived's Temakh) fundamentally changed, even impoverished, the world of magic for future generations. The setting makes it seem quite unlikely that anyone would ever even come close to rivalling Irem.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of humanity, some of them made relics. That's about it. The books show you these relics. A lot of them originate from more recent civilisations than Irem, and many of them were even made intentionally. As the books make it clear, what once could be churned out by formula by halls of craftsmen now takes single isolated occultists an entire lifetime to make. Irem was explicitly the greatest there has ever been, ruled by the children of the gods themselves. I don't know what there is about Mummy that gives you the impression that later civilisations would ever come close to those heights.<br /> <br /> Remember the themes of Mummy. Your heights are in your past. You are diminished now, in the present, and can barely even remember your own glory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:50:18-08:00","id":426163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426136#post426136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm much much more inclined to see them think the exact opposite of what you're trying to suggest.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you mean?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't entirely disagree with you, Azahul. I think there is room for more Lifeless, other Mummies originating from other cultures, but I <i>do</i> think those cultures should be tied to Irem's legacy somehow. Sorcerers in India might have heard of the mythical Rite of Return and sought to create their own liches, but only Ammut listened to their rituals and now these Indian Lifeless are the hounds of the shuankhsen - for example.<br /> <br /> And sure, maybe you say that's what fasad are for but like, I don't get it then...clearly the game was room to grow and have more content. It's like saying, &quot;What's wrong with the Seers for your Evil Mages? Why do we need all this additional material about left-handed legacies, Tremere, Mad, Banishers, and Scelesti?&quot; Well, because these antagonists represent different themes, and <b>Mummy</b> can do the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:50:30-08:00","id":426164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426156#post426156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember the themes of Mummy. <b>Your heights are in your past.</b> You are diminished now, in the present, and can barely even remember your own glory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't think of anything that would emphasize this more than the fear of being surpassed by a successor.<br /> <br /> &quot;We ruled the world... thousands of years ago.&quot; The Arisen cling to a delusion of being the nobles of an empire long dead and well beyond the grasp of Memory, Arisen and mortal alike. It's been a decline ever since the Rite of Return. You're a slave to a name buried for nearly countless ages; how hollow does it feel when you see something that makes you wonder if , just maybe, you have tied yourself utterly to something that <i>can be matched? </i><br /> <br /> I'm not asking for &quot;the Inca created Deathless that are ten times cooler than anything Irem made, &quot; nor am I wanting &quot;the Nameless Empire sucks and the modern day has it beat.&quot; But hints that Irem isn't the end-all, be-all of supernatural mojo and human ingenuity is massively in-theme for <i>Mummy</i>; it makes the Arisen doubt themselves and the worth of their eternal servitude. The point of Memory as a mechanic is that the Arisen should never be sure of anything; why is the complete and total supremacy of Irem a sacred cow, when <i>literally nothing else the Arisen 'know' </i>is?<br /> <br /> The nWoD is a toolkit. If you don't like an option, ignore it. But let it be there for those who think it could tell a neat story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:52:53-08:00","id":426167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426164#post426164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;We ruled the world... thousands of years ago.&quot; The Arisen cling to a delusion of being the nobles of an empire long dead and well beyond the grasp of Memory, Arisen and mortal alike.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arisen very explicitly weren't the aristocracy of Irem, dude. The nearest we get to that is the Mesen-Nebu's aesthetic, and even then they're <i>meritocratic alchemists.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The nWoD is a toolkit. If you don't like an option, ignore it. But let it be there for those who think it could tell a neat story. </div> </div> </div>The <i>djinni</i> is a lot harder to put back in the bottle than it is to conjure up from treasure and thin air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-03-2015, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:55:26-08:00","id":426174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426167#post426167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Arisen very explicitly weren't the aristocracy of Irem, dude. The nearest we get to that is the Mesen-Nebu's aesthetic, and even then they're <i>meritocratic alchemists.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I recall something in <i>Deceived</i> where it implied that the Arisen view themselves as noble, even though they were definitely not. Definitely could be wrong though!<br /> <br /> Either way, the Arisen view themselves as an essential part of the greatest thing humanity has ever made. If you can find me a punchy, one-word summary for that feeling, I'd be delighted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:57:00-08:00","id":426175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426147#post426147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Everything is either from Irem and awesome or not from Irem and shitty&quot; gets boring, much in the same way that Mage 1e suffered from &quot;everything is Atlantis.&quot; There's more to the world than the Nameless Empire and the 'failures' that have come since, and exploring some of that has a lot of potential. Sekhem is a <i>universal force</i>; Irem shouldn't have a monopoly on it, and certainly shouldn't be the only group of humans (or whatever the Shan'iatu were) to consciously interact with it. Show me what the rest of humankind has done in the ~6000 years we've had since Irem.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you really think the game line says &quot;Everything is either from Irem and awesome or not from Irem and shitty.&quot; You haven't been paying attention. Either way, I'll count myself glad I don't have to worry about playing at your table so I can play &quot;Setting Strawman Deconstruction:Electric Boogaloo.:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:59:30-08:00","id":426178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426167#post426167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>djinni</i> is a lot harder to put back in the bottle than it is to conjure up from treasure and thin air.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say this, and I'm struggling to find a reading other than &quot;options are bad!&quot;<br /> <br /> Werewolf is a game about spirits, but it's enhanced by adding the Pure as antagonists. Promethean is a game about being created, yet the Extempore are creatures of happenstance, rather than intent. Sometimes subversion is a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426175#post426175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you really think the game line says &quot;Everything is either from Irem and awesome or not from Irem and shitty.&quot; You haven't been paying attention. Either way, I'll count myself glad I don't have to worry about playing at your table so I can play &quot;Setting Strawman Deconstruction:Electric Boogaloo.:</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering when the personal attacks would come in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 03-03-2015, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:03:23-08:00","id":426182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426163#post426163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you mean?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't entirely disagree with you, Azahul. I think there is room for more Lifeless, other Mummies originating from other cultures, but I <i>do</i> think those cultures should be tied to Irem's legacy somehow. Sorcerers in India might have heard of the mythical Rite of Return and sought to create their own liches, but only Ammut listened to their rituals and now these Indian Lifeless are the hounds of the shuankhsen - for example.<br /> <br /> And sure, maybe you say that's what fasad are for but like, I don't get it then...clearly the game was room to grow and have more content. It's like saying, &quot;What's wrong with the Seers for your Evil Mages? Why do we need all this additional material about left-handed legacies, Tremere, Mad, Banishers, and Scelesti?&quot; Well, because these antagonists represent different themes, and <b>Mummy</b> can do the same</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, it's not the phrase &quot;new Lifeless&quot; that is getting my hackles up. It's &quot;new Mummies&quot;. There's plenty of room for new kinds of undead being in the world of Mummy, let's bear in mind that the term &quot;Lifeless&quot; includes the Amkhat, not just humanoid mummified creatures. I keep thinking of guardian statues and the permutations of the demons of Duat, for example. But when it comes to Mummies, I can't see what non-Iremite versions could possibly add to the game.<br /> <br /> Although in your example, yes, I would say that's what the Fasad are for. If only because the phrase &quot;Hound of the Shuankhsen&quot; is almost word for word the description given of the core book's sample Fasad.<br /> <br /> Also, I think TyrannicalRabbit is referring to the fact that the default position of an Arisen towards any form of Lifeless is condescending hostility, not faith-shattering awe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:03:43-08:00","id":426185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426163#post426163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you mean?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't entirely disagree with you, Azahul. I think there is room for more Lifeless, other Mummies originating from other cultures, but I <i>do</i> think those cultures should be tied to Irem's legacy somehow. Sorcerers in India might have heard of the mythical Rite of Return and sought to create their own liches, but only Ammut listened to their rituals and now these Indian Lifeless are the hounds of the shuankhsen - for example.<br /> <br /> And sure, maybe you say that's what fasad are for but like, I don't get it then...clearly the game was room to grow and have more content. It's like saying, &quot;What's wrong with the Seers for your Evil Mages? Why do we need all this additional material about left-handed legacies, Tremere, Mad, Banishers, and Scelesti?&quot; Well, because these antagonists represent different themes, and <b>Mummy</b> can do the same</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond the fact that this does not change one iota that each Arisen is going to have different ideas based on their current Descent and their general outlook and personality. A few places have shown them looking at certain Lifeless as lesser than what they are. Deconstruction of Irem is already built into the setting without tossing in a character type for literally no other reason than that. At MY table, If I toss in some odd new Lifeless type it wont be simply so I can have my players feel shitty for playing Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:06:36-08:00","id":426187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426178#post426178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say this, and I'm struggling to find a reading other than &quot;options are bad!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't understand the significance of not being able to un-publish something\u2026 well, I can only envy your lack of exposure to Exalted 2e and its attendant presentation issues. In the meantime, though, I sat through two years of that argument and I'm not putting up with a third; it's not something that really offers a fresh perspective.<br /> <br /> Done with that tangent. Holding onto hype for Sothis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:06:38-08:00","id":426188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426182#post426182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, <b>it's not the phrase &quot;new Lifeless&quot;</b> that is getting my hackles up. It's &quot;new Mummies&quot;. There's plenty of room for new kinds of undead being in the world of Mummy, let's bear in mind that the term &quot;Lifeless&quot; includes the Amkhat, not just humanoid mummified creatures. I keep thinking of guardian statues and the permutations of the demons of Duat, for example. But when it comes to Mummies, I can't see what non-Iremite versions could possibly add to the game.<br /> <br /> Although in your example, yes, I would say that's what the Fasad are for. If only because the phrase &quot;Hound of the Shuankhsen&quot; is almost word for word the description given of the core book's sample Fasad.<br /> <br /> Also, I think TyrannicalRabbit is referring to the fact that the default position of an Arisen towards any form of Lifeless is condescending hostility, not faith-shattering awe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here's my post that started this whole firestorm:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>There's been pretty explicit mention of later attempts at the Rite failing or creating Lifeless. <b>I'd love to see some of those Lifeless, especially with less emphasis on Iremite/Egyptian trappings.</b> </i></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:11:22-08:00","id":426189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426164#post426164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't think of anything that would emphasize this more than the fear of being surpassed by a successor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here, right off the bat, is that you're choosing one particular side of the two parts of the old age metaphor. Either the past is lost and can never be recovered, or the next generation is rising up to replace you and forget everything you have ever done.<br /> <br /> Mummy seems to have pretty conclusively gone with the former when it comes to magic. Once you have civilisations emulating Irem, even replacing it, you can no longer speak about what has been lost. And given that the central crux of all this is <i>Memory</i>, Mummy encourages a fear of loss a helluva lot more than it fears replacement.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426164#post426164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;We ruled the world... thousands of years ago.&quot; The Arisen cling to a delusion of being the nobles of an empire long dead and well beyond the grasp of Memory, Arisen and mortal alike. It's been a decline ever since the Rite of Return. You're a slave to a name buried for nearly countless ages; how hollow does it feel when you see something that makes you wonder if , just maybe, you have tied yourself utterly to something that <i>can be matched? </i><br /> <br /> I'm not asking for &quot;the Inca created Deathless that are ten times cooler than anything Irem made, &quot; nor am I wanting &quot;the Nameless Empire sucks and the modern day has it beat.&quot; But hints that Irem isn't the end-all, be-all of supernatural mojo and human ingenuity is massively in-theme for <i>Mummy</i>; it makes the Arisen doubt themselves and the worth of their eternal servitude. The point of Memory as a mechanic is that the Arisen should never be sure of anything; why is the complete and total supremacy of Irem a sacred cow, when <i>literally nothing else the Arisen 'know' </i>is?</div> </div> </div> </div>The modern world allows for a lot of very interesting questions to be posed, but they're subtly different from what you're describing. In many ways, the modern, mundane world has far surpassed Irem. What was once mighty magic known only to the Sesha-Hebsu (sending messages across vast distances) can now be done by anyone with a phone, to take one example. The world has many ways to make a Mummy feel small, awed, obsolete. However, it does this without removing Irem from its position as the &quot;sacred cow&quot; of magic, which allows the themes I described above to come into play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426164#post426164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nWoD is a toolkit. If you don't like an option, ignore it. But let it be there for those who think it could tell a neat story.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is hardly worth even addressing. The counter is &quot;The nWoD is a toolkit, with all the tools you need to enact the very themes you describe already. If you want to tell such a story, just use them.&quot; Like I said, see Immortals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:19:24-08:00","id":426197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426182#post426182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, it's not the phrase &quot;new Lifeless&quot; that is getting my hackles up. It's &quot;new Mummies&quot;. There's plenty of room for new kinds of undead being in the world of Mummy, let's bear in mind that the term &quot;Lifeless&quot; includes the Amkhat, not just humanoid mummified creatures. I keep thinking of guardian statues and the permutations of the demons of Duat, for example. But when it comes to Mummies, I can't see what non-Iremite versions could possibly add to the game.<br /> <br /> Although in your example, yes, I would say that's what the Fasad are for. If only because the phrase &quot;Hound of the Shuankhsen&quot; is almost word for word the description given of the core book's sample Fasad.<br /> <br /> Also, I think TyrannicalRabbit is referring to the fact that the default position of an Arisen towards any form of Lifeless is condescending hostility, not faith-shattering awe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this. Also while there are elements of wonder and awe with the accomplishments of Irem, even with consideration that it was a far far more brutal time than we the modern person and modern morality has to deal with. The setting is often a rumination on the trap of power and power vs identity,etc. It's simply not a setting built on a necessity to hammer into a player's head the idea that Irem wasn't anything unique and just badwrong. There are plenty of space for modern visions to look upon the necromancy, the brutality, the lies, the deceptions and conquests of Irem without bashing people over the head with Deathless of other civilizations. That the developer and co. stuck to their guns on this has been a relief. And I say that as someone who played Mummy, Mummy 2nd edition and Mummy: the Resurrection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:23:29-08:00","id":426204,"title":"","content":"Thankfully, I don't see <i>any </i>reason at all to assume that this book will have any info on non-Iremite mummies and on Sekhem sorcerers. <br /> <br /> In fact, we already know what the book will be about<b></b>: <br /> <br /> Sothis Ascends: This book examines the Sothic Turn; the cycle of existence that the Mummys live and die within. Since their creation, there have been five Turns and each is examined: one part historical setting, one part grab-bag of artifacts, powers, and antagonists. Also presents the final \u201cchapter\u201d of the three part adventure, with thematic content relating to the Turns. 160 pages. Aiming for January 20114 in PDF/PoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:24:14-08:00","id":426205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=425715#post425715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NON-IREMITE MUMMIES!</div> </div> </div> </div>FUCK THAT SHIT!<br /> <br /> Sorry, but I'm at such cross purposes with that. I love the logic of the series so far, with Iremite Mummies explaining mummy myths across the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426188#post426188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And here's my post that started this whole firestorm:<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, well, it skipped the part you quoted, but okay, that makes some sense. That might be cool. Still kinda opposed to it, but that's because I have a stick up my ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-03-2015, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:26:16-08:00","id":426209,"title":"","content":"Mummy is a game about identity. Shaking up the core tenant of the Arisen identity - <i>I am a product of the human race's greatest achievement, the likes of which will never even be approached, let alone matched </i>- is a terrifying idea, and one that I love. As I've said above, I don't want new Lifeless, but I do think that showing off Deathless independent of Iremite imitation should be disturbing enough to the average mummy to get some official wordcount. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:26:42-08:00","id":426210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426204#post426204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thankfully, I don't see <i>any </i>reason at all to assume that this book will have any info on non-Iremite mummies and on Sekhem sorcerers.<br /> <br /> In fact, we already know what the book will be about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Sothis Ascends: This book examines the Sothic Turn; the cycle of existence that the Mummys live and die within. Since their creation, there have been five Turns and each is examined: one part historical setting, one part grab-bag of artifacts, powers, and antagonists. Also presents the final \u201cchapter\u201d of the three part adventure, with thematic content relating to the Turns. 160 pages. Aiming for January 20114 in PDF/PoD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd just like to point out that included in that grab bag is &quot;antagonists&quot;, a label which could describe some (maybe not all) Sekhem sorcerers. So I'm going to hold out hope! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">I just hope I'll have enough money in my gaming budget for it when it gets released.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:28:34-08:00","id":426211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426204#post426204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thankfully, I don't see <i>any </i>reason at all to assume that this book will have any info on non-Iremite mummies and on Sekhem sorcerers.<br /> <br /> In fact, we already know what the book will be about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Sothis Ascends: This book examines the Sothic Turn; the cycle of existence that the Mummys live and die within. Since their creation, there have been five Turns and each is examined: one part historical setting, <b>one part grab-bag of artifacts, powers, and antagonists</b>. Also presents the final \u201cchapter\u201d of the three part adventure, with thematic content relating to the Turns. 160 pages. Aiming for January 20114 in PDF/PoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we're only getting this, Rio, and Dreams of Avarice after this, I think anything &quot;weird&quot; would end up in <i>Sothis</i>. I also feel like mortal sorcerers have gotten enough mention that never actually describing them seems like a bit of a waste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:28:53-08:00","id":426212,"title":"","content":"There's been quite a bit of talk about the book - <i>noone </i>who writes or develops for Onyx Path has said <i>anything</i> at all about Sekhem sorcerers being part of this book. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:29:44-08:00","id":426213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426188#post426188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And here's my post that started this whole firestorm:<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I was mostly responding to this post of yours:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=425715#post425715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NON-IREMITE MUMMIES!<br /> <br /> 90% of my hope for the book right there. That, along with moral sorcerers and the Roman \u00c6gyptus setting will sell me on this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:33:26-08:00","id":426214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426213#post426213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I was mostly responding to this post of yours:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies =/= Deathless.<br /> <br /> Shuankhsen are &quot;mummies,&quot; for one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:53:55-08:00","id":426229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426212#post426212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's been quite a bit of talk about the book - <i>noone </i>who writes or develops for Onyx Path has said <i>anything</i> at all about Sekhem sorcerers being part of this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone that writes for OP has said <i>anything</i> about this book, except for Gentleman Gamer saying he wrote about Mummy-eating cannibals for the Third Turn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T23:06:55-08:00","id":426234,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping for stories about Sekhem wielding sorcerers even if the mechanics end up being nothing more than the merits in Reliquary or the ones that those relic hunters in HtV get (just as an example - I'm not advocating hunter crossover or anything.) I have really been liking the tidbits we've been getting about them in Deceived and Guildhalls and want to hear about what happened to them and what they want. If we don't get that, it's fine. I've got plenty of ideas of my own (I put some in my signature). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do think that they've been mentioned for a reason.<br /> <br /> &quot;It came to pass that pressing east, we finally met Remet who imitated our customs with some skill. Instead of rough villages, these Ki-En-Gir built temples and cities. They prayed to false gods and wrote in a language they invented, instead of derived from the Nomenclature. A few saw through their false ways, however, and grasped some celestial knowledge. They were sorcerers and relicmakers who claimed to be one third divine. They led disciplined armies against us.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a lot there that appeals to me. I suspect that if they're ever detailed, they'll have limited power to make relics, and/or they'll have means to bind seba and unleash utterances (if only by stealing and using talismans.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 03-03-2015, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T23:43:39-08:00","id":426241,"title":"","content":"Totally psyched! New Mummy stuff is always a treat, but I've also been working on building a timeline of both the World of Darkness and general world history. I've found that the start of the Sothic Turns map to some particularly interesting periods (like the second turn starts twenty years after the Kingdom of Israel fragments into two counties, and one year after the rise of the Assyrians) so I'm totally jacked to see how that turns out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T00:19:11-08:00","id":426256,"title":"","content":"As Christian A mentioned, we have a rough blurb of this book and what to expect. <br /> <br /> Other then that, Reseru referenced Gentlemen Gamer mentioning Mummy eating antagonists in the Third Turn. <br /> <br /> We also have mention of Relic Architecture in DC and that it would be expanded in a future supplement. Considering Sothis seems a better place for that then Rio I'm hedging my bets that it will contain said rules expansion. Also from DC the White Jackal has an Utterance that still has not been published in any Mummy book, so I think that's likely to be in Sothis as well. <br /> <br /> I also remember an interview with CAS (might actually be under the Mummy tab on the Onyx Path website) that mentioned about adding new Lifeless who were knock-offs of the Rite of Return in Sothis. <br /> <br /> That's all that's been discussed or teased by the books or the devs I think. <br /> <br /> Now, with that out of the way the question is what would I like to see/hope to see?<br /> <br /> 1) Bane relics. <br /> 2) Demons of Duat as antagonists. <br /> 3) Sorcerers (need someone to summon said demons) <br /> 4) More relics<br /> 5) Some wordcount (not a huge amount, half a page sidebar would do) about running into other immortal characters across the turns/descents who are not Mummy's. Vampires and the three main types of Immortal from WoD:Immortals mainly. <br /> <br /> For that last point it mainly comes out of a comment on the old forums (or possibly an RPG.net) thread that was running while Mummy was in development that had a dev mention that the Purified from Immortals got a little quote or something about the Arisen and it was a statement of abject horror. Also, though I am less sure of this, I think before wordcount got cut down (so first draft of the book likely before redlines) there was going to be a sidebar or something on other immortals. So ever since I heard that got cut from the core I've kinda been hoping to see it get put somewhere and Sothis seems like the last place it could go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T00:50:27-08:00","id":426265,"title":"","content":"Is this thread really glitchy for anyone else? It keeps acting like it doesn't have a third page, gave me an error about the server when I tried to load it, and displays me with Hawthorn's avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T00:51:35-08:00","id":426268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426209#post426209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy is a game about identity. Shaking up the core tenant of the Arisen identity - <i>I am a product of the human race's greatest achievement, the likes of which will never even be approached, let alone matched </i>- is a terrifying idea, and one that I love. As I've said above, I don't want new Lifeless, but I do think that showing off Deathless independent of Iremite imitation should be disturbing enough to the average mummy to get some official wordcount.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you want a revenant?<br /> <br /> Because having a recently undead creature being consumed by overwhelming drive to go after something sounds exactly like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T02:36:26-08:00","id":426340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426265#post426265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this thread really glitchy for anyone else? It keeps acting like it doesn't have a third page, gave me an error about the server when I tried to load it, and displays me with Hawthorn's avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's happening for me, too.<br /> <br /> My list of desires basically mimics Hawthorn's. I'm really hoping that the book comes out before the <b>Dark Eras</b> backer surveys are sent out and my chapter expansion pitches are due, so I can see how <b>Sothis Ascends: Grab Bag of Mummy Goodies</b> adds to the game and what room I have left","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T03:03:38-08:00","id":426353,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify - while I incorporated the cannibal sorcerers of Ur in my draft (as reference to a group of Hunters in Mortal Remains) - I cannot comment as to their status in the finished book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Even I'm unsure of what has made the cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T03:04:50-08:00","id":426355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426340#post426340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's happening for me, too.<br /> <br /> My list of desires basically mimics Hawthorn's. I'm really hoping that the book comes out before the <b>Dark Eras</b> backer surveys are sent out and my chapter expansion pitches are due, so I can see how <b>Sothis Ascends: Grab Bag of Mummy Goodies</b> adds to the game and what room I have left</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by Kickstarter updates, they're probably going to contact the people with additions/expansions as soon as their payments are confirmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T03:18:15-08:00","id":426360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426355#post426355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by Kickstarter updates, they're probably going to contact the people with additions/expansions as soon as their payments are confirmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure my payment was confirmed thought and I've gotten nothing yet, so maybe they are waiting for Sothis to come out, or for all payments to be confirmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T03:23:52-08:00","id":426366,"title":"","content":"Would the First Turn, in the Old Kingdom, be contemporary to the Ancient Egypt info in Ancient Bloodlines/Ancient Mysteries, and Hunting Grounds: Sumer in the Werewolf Chronicler's Guide?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T03:36:29-08:00","id":426371,"title":"","content":"Seeing as the Hunting Grounds: Sumer is not contemporary with Ancient Egypt/Bloodlines/Mysteries...most likely not both.<br /> One or the other...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 03-03-2015, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T03:49:28-08:00","id":426387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426355#post426355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by Kickstarter updates, they're probably going to contact the people with additions/expansions as soon as their payments are confirmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>My payment has been confirmed already, but OP has already said they'll probably wait until next week. I don't think they'll be waiting for <b>Sothis</b><b> Ascends</b>, but I am! I'll hold out as long as I can.<br /> <br /> In my head-canon, <b>Werewolf</b> Sumer conveniently took place during the First Turn and the Khaibit bloodline was created in the Second Turn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T04:33:45-08:00","id":426434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426371#post426371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as the Hunting Grounds: Sumer is not contemporary with Ancient Egypt/Bloodlines/Mysteries...most likely not both.<br /> One or the other...</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Is the Sumerian one set earlier than I thought, because I know the height of Sumerian civlization and Old Kingdom Egypt overlapped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T05:38:17-08:00","id":426474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426434#post426434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Is the Sumerian one set earlier than I thought, because I know the height of Sumerian civlization and Old Kingdom Egypt overlapped.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know when the Ancient Bloodlines Egypt is set, but in regardsto Egypt and the City of Bau and the Dog Kings of Sumer, here's the time frame from another thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, a mention of the Sumerian King Gudea places the Chronicler's Guide setting somewhere in between 2144 and 2124 BC, so there's when Pharoh Neferkare predominantly ruled during this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T14:17:08-08:00","id":426986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426387#post426387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My payment has been confirmed already, but OP has already said they'll probably wait until next week. I don't think they'll be waiting for <b>Sothis</b><b> Ascends</b>, but I am! I'll hold out as long as I can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time's up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T15:45:19-08:00","id":427059,"title":"","content":"Shame. It would have been good to have seen what content is in Sothis before committing to an expansion for Dark Eras. Maybe you should try to wrangle a sneak preview, reseru?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426214#post426214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummies =/= Deathless.<br /> <br /> Shuankhsen are &quot;mummies,&quot; for one.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as I outlined earlier, my problem wasn't with &quot;Deathless&quot; or &quot;Lifeless&quot;, but with non-Iremite mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T15:52:16-08:00","id":427069,"title":"","content":"I will be utterly astonished if you get any mummies that aren't Iremite in origin in this gameline. The unmatched preeminence of Iremite magic is pretty central to the game. I say this as someone who wrote a good chunk on non-Egyptian mummy stuff for Mummy: The Resurrection.<br /> <br /> I suppose CAS could surprise me, but at no time ever has he even given the slightest hint that non-Iremite mummies were something he wanted to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T16:34:54-08:00","id":427098,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426212#post426212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's been quite a bit of talk about the book - <i>noone </i>who writes or develops for Onyx Path has said <i>anything</i> at all about Sekhem sorcerers being part of this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you be able to provide any links to the &quot;quite a bit of talk about the book&quot;? I just remember the mention of cannibals and the blurb you quoted, which reads:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426204#post426204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thankfully, I don't see <i>any </i>reason at all to assume that this book will have any info on non-Iremite mummies and on Sekhem sorcerers.<br /> <br /> In fact, we already know what the book will be about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Sothis Ascends: This book examines the Sothic Turn; the cycle of existence that the Mummys live and die within. Since their creation, there have been five Turns and each is examined: one part historical setting, one part grab-bag of artifacts, powers, and antagonists. Also presents the final \u201cchapter\u201d of the three part adventure, with thematic content relating to the Turns. 160 pages. Aiming for January 20114 in PDF/PoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note the word &quot;antagonists&quot;. Guildhalls of the Deathless, I think it was, made it sound very much like the Arisen Guilds are opposed to the idea of mortal sorcerers. Logically, that makes them antagonists, and thus a viable option under the book's synopsis.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T16:52:33-08:00","id":427112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=427069#post427069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will be utterly astonished if you get any mummies that aren't Iremite in origin in this gameline. The unmatched preeminence of Iremite magic is pretty central to the game. I say this as someone who wrote a good chunk on non-Egyptian mummy stuff for Mummy: The Resurrection.<br /> <br /> I suppose CAS could surprise me, but at no time ever has he even given the slightest hint that non-Iremite mummies were something he wanted to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I expected and wanted to hear, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T05:33:59-08:00","id":427631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=426986#post426986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time's up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://cs5844.vk.me/g30553934/a_89a3e775.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T16:31:09-07:00","id":434814,"title":"","content":"So, the phrase &quot;In a couple of weeks at most&quot; for the first proof is a little annoying.<br /> <br /> That said, this talk of maps has me rather intrigued. Maps of territories as they stood in prior Sothic Turns, I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T08:45:12-07:00","id":441354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=427098#post427098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note the word &quot;antagonists&quot;. Guildhalls of the Deathless, I think it was, made it sound very much like the Arisen Guilds are opposed to the idea of mortal sorcerers. Logically, that makes them antagonists, and thus a viable option under the book's synopsis.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we can assume they'll be antagonists tied to the wide sweep of Deathless history, so sorcerers inheriting a legacy that neither they nor the mummies truly remember - and often the manufacturers of the relics that mummies go looking for - don't seem to be an out-of-the-ass guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> (As for &quot;Deathless-level&quot; mummies from other civilisations, I think they'd be better rendered as completely different entities; if in a Mummy the Curse book at all, one analogous to Wicked Dead)<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, yes, psyched regardless.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I'm hoping for is expanded discussion - be it advice or mechanics - for what happens to a cult when it's left unattended for too long.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T18:58:40-07:00","id":462987,"title":"","content":"It seens it will be out this Wednesday!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T19:00:49-07:00","id":462990,"title":"","content":"I hate time zones. Every single time, I read that and go, &quot;Oh, tomorrow!&quot; and then have to remember that no, it'll be Thursday.<br /> <br /> Still psyched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-