forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:33:16-07:00","id":465232,"title":"","content":"Comment here, it's easier. It's not like this thread is overly bloated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:37:48-07:00","id":465251,"title":"","content":"I <i>love</i> that the intro fiction hints at the old African Olmec theory as being the result of Arisen meddling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:42:58-07:00","id":465260,"title":"","content":"Anyone else reading about the sha and suddenly thinking about the red-haired man from D.C.? I mean, they descend like Arisen... but it's a Sothic turn, and it's not theoretically impossible to stay at Sekhem 1 for another 4,000-odd years. Just really unlikely.<br /> <br /> From what I've skimmed, I get the impression that I'm not going to get any of what I was hoping for. No Relic Architecture rules (just a handful of different samples) and no set mechanics for sorcerers (but plenty more allusions to them manipulating Sekhem and definitely having powers of a kind). That's a bit disappointing. And I suspect a lot of my players will be truly frustrated at the absence of anything new for their characters on the Affinity/Utterance side, not counting the lone aforementioned Cosmic Utterance that can only be taken by members of a secret society none of them belong to. After all the juicy new rules that flooded the game in the Book of the Deceived and Guildhalls of the Deathless, it's a bit underwhelming at first glance. And 60 pages dedicated to the Avarice Chronicle chews up a lot of space.<br /> <br /> Ah well. Now to knuckle down and read it in depth. Hopefully the content that is there will be good enough to make up for the content I wish was there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:50:10-07:00","id":465276,"title":"","content":"I was never a hundred percent sure why y'all thought this would be a crunch heavy book.<br /> <br /> Honestly, given the Dark Eras rush I'm still getting off of, I feel like I'm getting another heavy snort of crack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:51:16-07:00","id":465282,"title":"","content":"Probably because there's a bunch of crunch referred to obliquely in the Mummy line that hasn't appeared in any form so far?<br /> <br /> I'm... genuinely really confused as to where the promised Relic Architecture rules are going to materialise now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:55:36-07:00","id":465290,"title":"","content":"Patience and faith, patience and faith. Enjoy what you have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:14:39-07:00","id":465303,"title":"","content":"Like I said in the initial post, that's my plan <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm sure it's excellent and well-written stuff, the Mummy line uniformly is. Just not really what I was looking for, particularly in the context of the campaigns I'm running where relic architecture was always meant to play a relatively significant part. Ah well, back to the cobbled together bunch of mechanics I've been working with so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:16:06-07:00","id":465305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=465282#post465282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably because there's a bunch of crunch referred to obliquely in the Mummy line that hasn't appeared in any form so far?<br /> <br /> I'm... genuinely really confused as to where the promised Relic Architecture rules are going to materialise now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rio maybe?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I agree with Arcane. There's a lot of very good historical content. It's like crack for me too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:21:07-07:00","id":465307,"title":"","content":"While there are a ton of things I want(need?) to see more of;Relic Architecture, Duat and the Judges of Duat, the Judges of Life, Ammut, Anpu, Azar, mortal Sekhem sorcerers, Cosmic Fate,etc. I wasn't expecting it in this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:31:55-07:00","id":465337,"title":"","content":"*shrug* A bit immaterial now, but it seemed like the obvious place to expect it. It's the final one of the main supplements and a book about different time periods would be the natural place for exploring gameplay elements that might require hundreds of years to lay foundations, shape the growth of entire cities, and guide the geometry of urban environments so that they match Iremite principles. The section on Interwoven Chronicles actually has gameplay ideas for exactly that kind of play... but Relic Architecture itself is missing. And mortal Sekhem Sorcerer rules would have been natural because, well, just look at how many times mortal Sekhem sorcerers come up in the course of the book. They're all over the place, they're just lacking any mechanics to allow for their actual use outside of buying blue book supplements.<br /> <br /> Duat, Judges, Ammut, Anpu, Azar, Fate, etc. aren't anything I ever expected from this book. Half of that seems like it would be natural for Dreams of Avarice to look at, the rest would be content for the speculative Book of Going Westward. And Rio is the only place I can imagine Relic Architecture showing up now, but sticking something like that into a setting book is a bit weird. Maybe another supplement in the vein of Lore of the Deceived, perhaps? I'll live in hope. In the meantime, back to readjusting my expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T17:04:03-07:00","id":465348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=465337#post465337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug* A bit immaterial now, but it seemed like the obvious place to expect it. It's the final one of the main supplements and a book about different time periods would be the natural place for exploring gameplay elements that might require hundreds of years to lay foundations, shape the growth of entire cities, and guide the geometry of urban environments so that they match Iremite principles. The section on Interwoven Chronicles actually has gameplay ideas for exactly that kind of play... but Relic Architecture itself is missing. And mortal Sekhem Sorcerer rules would have been natural because, well, just look at how many times mortal Sekhem sorcerers come up in the course of the book. They're all over the place, they're just lacking any mechanics to allow for their actual use outside of buying blue book supplements.<br /> <br /> Duat, Judges, Ammut, Anpu, Azar, Fate, etc. aren't anything I ever expected from this book. Half of that seems like it would be natural for Dreams of Avarice to look at, the rest would be content for the speculative Book of Going Westward. And Rio is the only place I can imagine Relic Architecture showing up now, but sticking something like that into a setting book is a bit weird. Maybe another supplement in the vein of Lore of the Deceived, perhaps? I'll live in hope. In the meantime, back to readjusting my expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>While a somewhat reasonable expectation. The last of specifically pitching Relic Architecture in the book promo before release was a big indication to me that it wasn't going to be in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T17:11:54-07:00","id":465354,"title":"","content":"I'm about 36 pages in, and I'm satisfied by the support for Sekhem sorcerers so far. There's no character generator for them, but this gives us a lot of the missing pieces of their lore. (I have heretical theories about the Mesopotamian sorcerers). Tempted to make a doc assembling all the Iremite powers a mortal can command at some point. For now, more Sothis!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T17:45:49-07:00","id":465394,"title":"","content":"I'm currently in the first Turn(haven't even glanced ahead).<br /> All I can say it is probably the most exciting period for the Arisen ever!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T17:48:45-07:00","id":465396,"title":"","content":"Wait until you get to the Second Turn.<br /> <br /> History is putty in your hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T17:50:07-07:00","id":465399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=465260#post465260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've skimmed, I get the impression that I'm not going to get any of what I was hoping for. No Relic Architecture rules (just a handful of different samples) and no set mechanics for sorcerers (but plenty more allusions to them manipulating Sekhem and definitely having powers of a kind). That's a bit disappointing. And I suspect a lot of my players will be truly frustrated at the absence of anything new for their characters on the Affinity/Utterance side, not counting the lone aforementioned Cosmic Utterance that can only be taken by members of a secret society none of them belong to. After all the juicy new rules that flooded the game in the Book of the Deceived and Guildhalls of the Deathless, it's a bit underwhelming at first glance. And 60 pages dedicated to the Avarice Chronicle chews up a lot of space.<br /> <br /> Ah well. Now to knuckle down and read it in depth. Hopefully the content that is there will be good enough to make up for the content I wish was there.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are my thoughts as well. The initial blurb given about the book promised loads of relics, powers, and antagonists but an initial skim is just showing a lot of words saying, &quot;Here's what the Guilds are up to.&quot;<br /> <br /> Even the beginning of the book states that Sothic turns are periods where all kinds of magic and Fate-inspired events take place, but (again, initial skim) the only chapter that really seems to uphold that is the first one, which of course has all kinds of cool unique hooks in it because <i>it's the first one</i>. Other than talking about the three phases of the Turn, there's a very subtle sort of campaign structure or story in the first chapter, too. I hope the other two follow suit but it didn't seem it right away. But that's historical gaming done right, like <b>King Arthur Pendragon</b>: there's a story unfolding in the world and your character takes part.<br /> <br /> The SAS seems long, too.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I'm really impressed by the first chapter but it looks like I'll have to read more closely into the other ones if I'm hoping to be similarly blown away<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T18:16:34-07:00","id":465429,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, it looks like the Faithful of Shulpae are the creation of a shuankhsen. I figured as much, but it's neat to see it in clearer terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T18:20:04-07:00","id":465432,"title":"","content":"So far only as far as page 20. The First Turn chapter so far is excellent with a nice sidebar on the names of places and gods. Glad to see the Sphinx and it's effects mentioned again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T18:25:10-07:00","id":465436,"title":"","content":"Hum, just finished the 1st chapter. It was really well written, with a lot of good ideas, historical content and really really exciting. You can easily picture how life in Khemet was at the time and how you can fit in the Arisen there(and even some other lands information). I hope the other chapters are as well written as this one.<br /> Seens that King Unas formed the basis that would later be the Faithful of Shulpae.<br /> <br /> About Sekhem Sorcerers: Well it seens that indeed we have rules about them. They can create Relics and Ankhata, but hardly the miracles the Arisen can perform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 04-01-2015, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T18:52:30-07:00","id":465451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=465429#post465429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh hey, it looks like the Faithful of Shulpae are the creation of a shuankhsen. I figured as much, but it's neat to see it in clearer terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I ran them as a Devourer cult in my game. Pretty natural route to go with them, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T19:15:27-07:00","id":465474,"title":"","content":"Not directly related to Sothis Ascends but a picture a friend recently showed me that just made me laugh and think about the Shan'iatu and the Judges of Life. <img src=\"https://scontent-sea.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfa1/v/t1.0-9/984298_1066173043409241_2502008838375967839_n.jpg?oh=46bc0c4e69022962a792332fd6fdc547&amp;oe=55ADC11F\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T19:23:56-07:00","id":465497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=465436#post465436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hum, just finished the 1st chapter. It was really well written, with a lot of good ideas, historical content and really really exciting. You can easily picture how life in Khemet was at the time and how you can fit in the Arisen there(and even some other lands information). I hope the other chapters are as well written as this one.<br /> Seens that King Unas formed the basis that would later be the Faithful of Shulpae.<br /> <br /> About Sekhem Sorcerers: Well it seens that indeed we have rules about them. They can create Relics and Ankhata, but hardly the miracles the Arisen can perform.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I imagined as such. They are a lesser template, after all, particularly given how the Shan'iatu deliberately hoarded a lot of their tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T19:34:52-07:00","id":465504,"title":"","content":"Reading Chapter 2, halfway along it. So far it seens to be like Game of Thrones but Arisen flavoured. Most of the ancient Empires around with Egypt not as prominent as before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T19:36:57-07:00","id":465505,"title":"","content":"You know, the mystery of Imhotep is really going to amuse one of my Deceived players, given that he opted for to take that name for his character and the vague suppositions about some connection to the Lost Guild...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T20:40:16-07:00","id":465558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=465396#post465396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait until you get to the Second Turn.<br /> <br /> History is putty in your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>History is Elmer's glue.<br /> <br /> Sticky, Gets everywhere, and tastes bad when you eat it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T00:03:16-07:00","id":465746,"title":"","content":"Just finished the book and I'm pretty pleased overall. It's not the same level of crazy good that Book of the Deceived was (though Dreams of Avarice may well match up), but it's still a damn good book.<br /> <br /> The settings are the bulk of the book, and they range in quality. The First Turn is definitely the best of the three, as it rather clearly lays out several plot threads and provides a very cinematic view of a time far removed from our own while still being very playable; it makes me want to start my next chronicle during. The Second Turn is probably the weakest, throwing out a lot of shallow info about the mortal world while not really offering enough to be compelling as chronicle material. At times, it feels downright textbook-y, which is a death sentence for historical content to just about anyone but a dedicated student, and I feel like it could've benefited from a tighter narrative focus. Turn Three is interesting in that it shakes up Arisen culture and offers a whole host of weird factions that tie in well into history and all act as satisfying threads for a story, but doesn't ever lead it to a real point, instead just offering a Storyteller a lot of things to extensively build off of.<br /> <br /> The section on Storyteller advice is essential and should've been in core; it's incredibly well-written and offers tons of pointers for running a game as complex as Mummy, in terms of flashbacks and setting weirdness. The structure of an &quot;Interwoven Chronicle&quot; and the suggestions that the Arisen don't operate linearly with time are great inspiration that will see a ton of use.<br /> <br /> Overall, the book is very light on mechanics, offering a handful of NPC statblocks and one new Utterance that I can only see either being banned or required for a chronicle. I wasn't terribly fond of the final bit of the Avarice Chronicle, but I haven't loved the rest of it either, so results may vary. <br /> <br /> The lack of lore revelations surprised me; for a book that pulls back the curtain on Memory, there was unexpectedly little in terms of facts that really shake things up or even hints towards mythology.<br /> <br /> Sothis Ascends is solid; not amazing, not bad. You'll either use everything in it or probably ignore 90% of the book, but if the premise interests you at all, grab it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T02:59:53-07:00","id":465854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=465505#post465505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the mystery of Imhotep is really going to amuse one of my Deceived players, given that he opted for to take that name for his character and the vague suppositions about some connection to the Lost Guild...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Imhotep was a maddening thing to write about, because as Malcolm and I point out in the first Turn his life story falls outside the experience of any mummy - the long henet is a hard fact of the setting, so he *couldn't* be a mummy... Or could he?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T07:53:19-07:00","id":466084,"title":"","content":"Just read the Fourth Chapter. Had really good storytelling advice.<br /> Of the Turns my favorite was the First and the Second the least.<br /> Now reading the Adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T09:00:43-07:00","id":466175,"tit