in-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=466604#post466604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alas, I lacked the space, but I'll aim to post a stat block here with some of their odd powers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that would really be nice! Looking forward to it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 04-02-2015, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:11:23-07:00","id":466850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=466564#post466564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Imhotep had anything to do with the Awakened, but I do think <i>some </i>of the sorcerers of Ki-En-Gir might have been the Awakened Scelesti of Kish referenced in Left-Hand Path.<br /> <br /> BotD: &quot;...<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">these Ki-En-Gir built temples and cities. They prayed to false gods and wrote in a language they invented, instead of derived from the Nomenclature. A few saw through their false ways, however, and grasped some celestial knowledge. They were sorcerers and relicmakers who claimed to be one third divine. They led disciplined armies against us.</span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> That seemed like a reference to High Speech, but I didn't realize until Sothis Ascends that the Ki-En-Gir encompassed Kish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know if this was intended or not. Mummy has steared far from crossover so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T22:19:58-07:00","id":467007,"title":"","content":"Seems more like First Tongue to me. Still going to remain ambiguous though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T00:06:32-07:00","id":467078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=466850#post466850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't know if this was intended or not. Mummy has steared far from crossover so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>If intended, I doubt it will ever be confirmed. That's ok by me; I like the mysterious hints and hooks peppering Mummy books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T00:26:28-07:00","id":467083,"title":"","content":"Agreed. It's nice to stumble across a nod or too, but a straight-up crossover is not something that should be found in the core of the line. SA is part of the core Mummy line. Mortal Remains, Necropolis: DC, Necropolis: Rio, Dreams of Avarice, Dark Eras &amp; (if we're lucky) the Book of Going Westward won't be, so I expect to find more weirdness in them.<br /> <br /> It'd be like having the rules for a new Changeling Seeming in a Forsaken book, because it ties into spirits. I admit that's an exaggeration, but given how much they've been trumpeting 'Mummy is a self-contained game with no crossover references', I feel it is a fair point to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T00:41:36-07:00","id":467090,"title":"","content":"Beyond the Deceived angle..I think in my headcanon this might involve the Judges of Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T05:04:07-07:00","id":467227,"title":"","content":"Making a batch of Affinities relating to specific splats is on my to-do list.<br /> <br /> I've been saying we needed a <b>Night Horrors</b> book since the core book came out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T05:27:09-07:00","id":467246,"title":"","content":"A Night Horrors book and Book of Going Westward are on my wishlist for Mummy. Hope to see them one day for Mummy, Before or after a Second Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T05:51:42-07:00","id":467258,"title":"","content":"I agree, but then I have been going out of my way to buy each of the Mummy books in both pdf &amp; P.O.D. format in the hopes that the line might get an extension.<br /> Not exactly an unbiased source. But very much in favour of a <b>Night Horrors</b> for the Arisen. It could include;<ul><li>Odd &amp;/or Old Amkhata</li> <li>Established 'Nome-Allied' Deceived</li> <li>'Sympathetic' Shuankhsen</li> <li>Mortal Sorcerer Relic Thief</li> <li>Last Dynasty International Capture Team</li> <li>The Demons of Duat</li> <li>Rival Arisen</li> </ul><br /> All of which already are inside the lore of the game. None of which would require something overly dramatic, more like Immortal Sinners rather than Wicked Dead. That's just off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Not to mention we do need more Utterances, to expand the number of 'source-book keywords' in use, (like Cosmic &amp; Unison).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:03:28-07:00","id":467266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=467258#post467258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but then I have been going out of my way to buy each of the Mummy books in both pdf &amp; P.O.D. format in the hopes that the line might get an extension.<br /> Not exactly an unbiased source. But very much in favour of a <b>Night Horrors</b> for the Arisen. It could include;<ul><li>Odd &amp;/or Old Amkhata</li> <li>Established 'Nome-Allied' Deceived</li> <li>'Sympathetic' Shuankhsen</li> <li>Mortal Sorcerer Relic Thief</li> <li>Last Dynasty International Capture Team</li> <li>The Demons of Duat</li> <li>Rival Arisen</li> </ul><br /> <br /> All of which already are inside the lore of the game. None of which would require something overly dramatic, more like Immortal Sinners rather than Wicked Dead. That's just off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Not to mention we do need more Utterances, to expand the number of 'source-book keywords' in use, (like Cosmic &amp; Unison).</div> </div> </div> </div>We could add some other Lifeless beings to that list! I prefer it than sample NPCs actually.<br /> Maybe we could get some kind of &quot;Lore of the Arisen&quot; book, that include more affinities and Utterances and also gives us some other &quot;magic stuff&quot; like geomancy rules and other types of magic experimentation among the Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:45:29-07:00","id":467315,"title":"","content":"About the Night Horrors idea: I would prefer it that way myself! I was just pointing out that they have options already available. I hope to quietly convince the Devs to take it up as a project. Pointing out the distinctly non-destructive effect on the 'meta' aspects of the game.<br /> <br /> About the Lore of the Arisen concept: I love this idea! By the pricking of my thumbs, I would love to get my hands on that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T07:15:27-07:00","id":467342,"title":"","content":"I do like all those ideas, but I still would prefer more of a <b>Wicked Dead</b> than <b>Immortal Sinners</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:17:29-07:00","id":467555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/425677-who-s-getting-psyched-for-sothis-ascends?p=466251#post466251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the apples of the Strangers seen to work on a similar principle as their products. They just use it for different goals.<br /> And about LDI and Cheiron...<br /> Well Cheiron is good but hasn't monopolized the market of hunting and producing products out of supernaturals creatures bodies yet...</div> </div> </div> </div>Same resource, different uses.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the cost analysis building stuff to target the Arisen when you have a much more common target within your grasp.<br /> <br /> &quot;For every one Arisen, we could've brought in ten Kindred with almost the same effect and much lower cost to boot! Let LDI deal with the Arisen, we'll undercut them in terms of cost.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:25:31-07:00","id":467739,"title":"","content":"Also, I wouldn't mind to see something on the vein of Sothis Ascends again, envolving different Eras that brings something unique, like mummies in the Incan Empire and China, after all historical gameplaying is Mummy forte, also I am a History addict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T13:13:59-07:00","id":467825,"title":"","content":"Chinese is possible, but I think the Incan thing is really even more unlikely than it was before Sothis Ascends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T13:38:49-07:00","id":467834,"title":"","content":"*something* in the east caused the darkness to spread in advance of the Third Turn...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthe